{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Will I not silence his limbs?</b> — I will not silence [from] telling." "<b>His limbs</b> — it returns to the preceding, like \"your limbs\" [בדיך]. And if he prevails over me, I will not silence [from] telling his might." "<b>And the grace of his array</b> — from the root of מצא חן (found favor). And some say: <b>his limbs</b> returns to Leviathan, from the root of בתים (rooms) [as] chambers [בדים], and the first is closer to me."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:35.389762912Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}